name issue_152_link_allocation_v2
describe A clean 4 Mbps link with every v2 switch on: video at its 2.5 Mbps maximum is encoded at the maximum, as libwebrtc's link_allocation headroom allows (#152)
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=4000kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
packetization v2
rtx v2
keyframe v2
pacer v2
cc v2
audio v2
allocator v2
# VideoSendStreamImpl::OnBitrateUpdated takes link_allocation (payload - protection) before
# capping the encoder target at the encoder maximum, so with an allocation above 2.5 Mbps the
# EncoderBitrateAdjuster has headroom and does not trim the encoder below its maximum.
# Seeds 1-5: video.avg_kbps main 2378-2394, with the fix 2442-2463. libwebrtc encodes
# 2.5 Mbps at a 2.5 Mbps target on `cross_traffic` before the competing flow (310627 bytes in
# second 10 of `parity-data/traces/cross_traffic.1.webrtc.video.csv`, ours 300697 before, 310627 after).
expect video.avg_kbps > 2420
expect video.freeze_count == 0
